Original commit body from ab67ad3ae7c0f8dac2e54010d95b18b3b31ef397:

ADR-0057 §1 rules that a producer which did not observe an attribute
contributes no candidate for it, and for nine of the ten attributes the
merge pass tracks the VALUE says so: the `Symbol` default is None, "" or
[] and `_candidates` already skipped it, per record. `is_exported: bool =
False` cannot — a default False is indistinguishable from a measured one
— so both SCIP arms, which assign the field nowhere, contributed a
phantom `False` candidate on every record they emitted: on the recorded
aardvark-dns fixture, 41 contests that arbitration then resolved and 107
agreements reported as two producers concurring. All of it read as
evidence in the one table §5 lets change an arbitration default.

The cure is a declaration on the §10 producer contract, not a change to
arbitration, which was right. `MergeAnchor.observes` names which of the
abstention-blind attributes a backend computes;
`ABSTENTION_BLIND_ATTRIBUTES` is DERIVED from `Symbol`'s field defaults,
so a tracked attribute that gains a concrete default appears there the
day it is added; declaring an attribute that does express absence by
value is refused at construction. `observes=None` is not a ruling: the
merge pass takes no candidate from such a producer and the live-registry
contract test refuses any shipped anchored producer that left it unset.

Declared: `rust` and `python` compute exportedness (pub modifiers;
`__all__` and the underscore convention); `rust_analyzer` and
`scip_python` compute none.

Measured: aardvark-dns `is_exported` (107, 41, 0, 0) -> (0, 0, 148, 0);
scip-python sample (4, 6, 0, 0) -> (0, 0, 10, 0). Every other attribute
row, the pairing and the edge overlap are unchanged, and no carried value
moves — only the provenance the artifact claims for it. Four mutants
killed, including leaving a shipped producer unruled.

Filed rather than swept in: INV-kubup (the artifact still asserts
`is_exported: false` wherever the analyzer has no rule, which finalize
entrenches and the dead-code seed set reads) and INV-nudoj (`Edge`'s
concrete defaults are the same family, unaudited).

Closes INV-huboz

